  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line 2 large oven trays with baking paper. Thinly slice the capsicums. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Drain and rinse the corn and beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495207/photos/large/prep_ingredients-8c8caa8de00070e4b0cee8d7cc0f9a9a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook filling: Combine the Tex-Mex seasoning, 1 tsp sugar and 1 tbs hot water in a bowl. Heat 1 tbs olive oil in a large deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the capsicum, stirring occasionally, for 5-6 mins until softened. Add the spice mixture, corn, beans and garlic (see Feed A Crowd) and cook, stirring and slightly mashing the beans, for 2 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495208/photos/large/soften_capsicum-2d813e7ced96a6a33f8599bc31f84284.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make quesadillas: Transfer the bean mixture to a large bowl. Add the spinach and stir until the spinach is wilted. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the bean mixture among the tortillas, then crumble over the feta. Fold the tortillas over to enclose the filling, then press together firmly.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495209/photos/large/make_quesadillas-5d5c855847da4ba0a6262db6e8faca41.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake quesadillas: Put the quesadillas on the lined trays and lightly spray or brush with olive oil. Bake, swapping the trays halfway, for 10-12 mins until golden and crisp.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495210/photos/large/bake_quesadillas-e6fc0369b6bb0dcaabe040701fe3db6a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the quesadillas among plates and serve with mayonnaise, if using. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495211/photos/large/serve_up-9a85b88cf2fa73c347255006bacc9ed1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Feed A Crowd: If you like a kick of heat, add a pinch of chilli flakes to the bean mixture, or scatter over to serve if it's just for you.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/495212/photos/large/feed_a_crowd-ec0629a8e60c12157bcc9218b51a8aab.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
